With the vault inside the repo and the tier pinned to `path: specs`, `--tier project` creates
`{repo}/specs/` and its README, then the symlink `{vault}/specs -> {repo}/specs`; `readlink`
asserts the link's target.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/config.yaml --
core:
  specs:
    tiers:
      project:
        path: specs
-- cmd --
booping specs init --tier project
readlink vault/specs
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
created dir {CWD}/specs
created file {CWD}/specs/README.md
linked {CWD}/vault/specs -> {CWD}/specs
{CWD}/specs
{CWD}/specs
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/specs/README.md --
# specs/

This project's specs tier: values, rules, ADRs and the other typed records, in booping's specs format — the guide is `src/specs/README.md` in the booping plugin. Check with `booping specs check --tier project`.
